```hbs
<section class="topic-kpi-section" aria-labelledby="kpi-topic-heading">
  <h2 id="kpi-topic-heading" class="kpi-topic-title">suggested KPIs for this topic</h2>

  <p class="kpi-topic-intro">
    These KPIs help teams gather, organize, and apply competitor intelligence in ways that
    strengthen strategic planning, proposal development, win themes, and business development
    decision-making.
  </p>

  <div class="expandable-container kpi-expandable-container">

    <!-- 1. Intelligence Collection -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-ci-collection">
        intelligence collection &amp; market awareness
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
             viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
                   points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-ci-collection">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Track project awards involving key competitors each month.</li>
          <li>Monitor competitor websites, LinkedIn activity, and industry news on a scheduled basis.</li>
          <li>Capture competitor observations from conferences, client conversations, and debriefs.</li>
          <li>Maintain RSS feeds covering competitors, markets, and target sectors.</li>
          <li>Document strategic hires, mergers, acquisitions, and new service offerings as they occur.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. Analysis & Interpretation -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-ci-analysis">
        analysis, interpretation &amp; competitor profiling
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
             viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
                   points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-ci-analysis">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Maintain current profiles for all major competitors.</li>
          <li>Update competitor strengths, weaknesses, and strategic priorities quarterly.</li>
          <li>Identify recurring market, service, and geographic patterns among competitors.</li>
          <li>Distinguish documented facts from assumptions and opinions.</li>
          <li>Review competitor profiles before major strategic planning sessions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. Intelligence Management -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-ci-management">
        intelligence management &amp; organizational memory
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
             viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
                   points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-ci-management">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Assign ownership for maintaining competitor intelligence records.</li>
          <li>Ensure observations are recorded within two weeks of discovery.</li>
          <li>Capture intelligence from proposal debriefs and client interviews.</li>
          <li>Store competitor intelligence in a searchable, centralized location.</li>
          <li>Review intelligence repositories regularly for completeness and relevance.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. Strategic Application -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-ci-application">
        strategic planning, proposals &amp; differentiation
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
             viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
                   points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-ci-application">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Include competitor intelligence discussions in strategic planning meetings.</li>
          <li>Evaluate likely competitors during proposal kickoff meetings.</li>
          <li>Apply the Step 9 differentiation test during win theme development.</li>
          <li>Use competitor intelligence during Blue Team and Red Team reviews.</li>
          <li>Track how often competitor intelligence influences proposal strategy, teaming decisions, or go/no-go decisions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <p class="kpi-topic-footer">
    Competitor intelligence creates value only when it influences decisions. Collect it,
    analyze it, preserve it, and use it to build stronger strategies, stronger proposals,
    and stronger reasons for clients to choose your organization.
  </p>
</section>
